      ":question/problem": "![](images/d2/d250f01dd1dd09c64ac802095741afdf5d2644b24efca65f5cbf6bc448371b54.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $XYZW$ is a parallelogram.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> $XY = ZW$\n\nThe table below gives the proof of the statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $XYZW$ is a parallelogram | {{field-1}} |\n| 2 | $WY^(\u2015)\u2245WY^(\u2015)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| 3 | $WX^(\u2015)\u2225YZ^(\u2015)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| 4 | $\u2220WYZ\u2245\u2220XWY$ | {{field-4}} |\n| 5 | $XY^(\u2015)\u2225WZ^(\u2015)$ | {{field-5}} |\n| 6 | $\u2220XYW\u2245\u2220YWZ$ | {{field-6}} |\n| 7 | $\u25b3WXY\u2245\u25b3YZW$ | {{field-7}} |\n| 8 | $XY^(\u2015)\u2245ZW^(\u2015)$ | {{field-8}} |\n| 9 | $XY = ZW$ | {{field-9}} |"
    },
