      ":question/problem": "![](images/53/5312c5dda506ab69a21888264c694ebdd0dbb0a147fe45823444f7c63ee45c93.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, $LMNP$ is a parallelogram.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> $m\u2220L = m\u2220N$\n\nThe table below gives the proof of the statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $LMNP$ is a parallelogram | {{field-1}} |\n| 2 | $MN^(\u2015)\u2225LP^(\u2015)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| 3 | $ML^(\u2015)\u2225NP^(\u2015)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| 4 | $\u2220NMP\u2245\u2220LPM$ | {{field-4}} |\n| 5 | $\u2220LMP\u2245\u2220NPM$ | {{field-5}} |\n| 6 | $MP^(\u2015)\u2245MP^(\u2015)$ | {{field-6}} |\n| 7 | $\u25b3MLP\u2245\u25b3PNM$ | {{field-7}} |\n| 8 | $\u2220L\u2245\u2220N$ | {{field-8}} |\n| 9 | $m\u2220L = m\u2220N$ | {{field-9}} |"
